From 2e677db82c4b12a713d5bdfc08c6575a58dfa089 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:44:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/17] uhf: add missing parcelable declaration files for the
 AIDL interfaces

Every custom Parcelable referenced from an AIDL interface needs a
matching <ClassName>.aidl declaration file (`parcelable ClassName;`) in
the same package - without one, the aidl compiler cannot resolve the
import and IUhfService.aidl fails to compile at all. Missing since the
first Phase 1 commit; found by actually running the aidl compiler and
javac against this package for the first time (prebuilts/build-tools
aidl + prebuilts/sdk/34/system/android.jar were available in this
environment, so this was verified for real rather than by inspection).

With these seven files added, the aidl compiler generates
IUhfService/IUhfTagCallback/IUhfStateCallback cleanly, and the entire
android.hardware.uhf package - all Parcelables, UhfManager, UhfSession,
TagFilter, TagCallback, UhfException, and the three generated AIDL
interfaces - compiles against the real system-API stub jar with zero
errors (one expected miss, Context.UHF_SERVICE, because the prebuilt
stub jar predates this local edit to Context.java - confirmed to be the
only issue by substituting a literal in a scratch copy and recompiling).

This is the strongest verification this framework layer has had in this
series: real javac/aidl output, not cross-referencing scripts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
